# Cursor AI Rules for apps/web

> **Extends:** [Root .cursorrules](../../.cursorrules)

## App Context

This is the **public-facing web application** for Xala/Digilist Platform.

**Critical:** Most pages are PUBLIC (no authentication required).

## Web-Specific Rules

### 1. Public Access Pattern
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Optional authentication
import { useAuth } from '@digilist/client-sdk/hooks';

function PublicPage() {
  const { user } = useAuth(); // user may be null

  return (
    <div>
      {user ? <AuthenticatedView /> : <PublicView />}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 2. Performance First
- Code split routes with `React.lazy()`
- Lazy load heavy components (maps, calendars)
- Use `loading="lazy"` for images
- Optimize bundle size (<300KB main chunk)

### 3. Mobile-First Design
- All tap targets minimum 44x44px
- Test on mobile viewport first
- Use responsive images (srcset)
- Touch-friendly interactions

### 4. SEO Requirements
```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED for public pages
import { Helmet } from 'react-helmet-async';

function ListingPage({ listing }) {
  return (
    <>
      <Helmet>
        <title>{listing.title} | Xala</title>
        <meta name="description" content={listing.description} />
        <meta property="og:title" content={listing.title} />
        <meta property="og:image" content={listing.imageUrl} />
      </Helmet>
      {/* Page content */}
    </>
  );
}
```

## File Organization

```
src/
├── features/
│   ├── listings/     # Listing discovery
│   ├── booking/      # Booking flows
│   └── search/       # Search & filters
├── routes/           # Page components
├── components/       # Shared components
└── main.tsx          # Entry point
```

## Testing

- E2E tests: `../../tests/e2e/web-*.spec.ts`
- Unit tests: Co-located `*.test.tsx`

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

❌ Requiring auth on public pages
❌ Hardcoding strings (use i18n)
❌ Direct API calls (use SDK)
❌ Importing from `@digdir/*` (use `@xala/ds`)
❌ Large bundle sizes (split code)

## SDK Services

Primary hooks used in this app:
- `useListings()` - Listing search
- `useListingDetails()` - Single listing
- `useAvailability()` - Check dates
- `useBooking()` - Create booking
- `useCategories()` - Category list

